tblWarm = input.int(6, "Warm-up — confirmed events a timeframe needs before it reports", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gTbl, tooltip = "How many confirmed BOS / CHOCH events a timeframe's own simulation must have produced before its row is allowed to report a trend. Until then all three of its cells read as no trend.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. Every row above the chart's own timeframe is computed by request.security, which sees only as much history of that timeframe as the chart has loaded. The engine starts from the first bar it is given and its opening range is anchored on the extreme of THAT window, so a short window can settle into a different structure from the real one. That is why the same 1M row could read BULLISH from one chart timeframe and BEARISH from another.\n\nThe engine forgets where it started once enough events have gone by. Measured over 500 randomised series against full-history truth: 63% agreement after one confirmed event, 91% after four, 98% after seven, and effectively exact by eleven. 6 is a deliberate middle — it removes almost all of the disagreement while keeping rows populated on ordinary history.\n\nRaise it if you want the table to speak only when it is certain. Set it to 0 to switch the gate off and see the raw per-timeframe reading, which is what every build before v15.16 showed.\n\nThe row for the chart's OWN timeframe is never gated: it reports the on-chart engine, which always has the full loaded history.")
